Input:
Write a Java function `public static int[][] inverseMatrix(int[][] matrix)` to find the inverse of a matrix.

Example:
>>> inverseMatrix(new int[][] {{1, 2}, {3, 4}})
{{-2, 1}, {1.5, -0.5}}
Output:
```
public static int[][] inverseMatrix(int[][] matrix) {
    int n = matrix.length;
    int[][] result = new int[n][n];
    int det = determinant(matrix);
    if (det == 0) {
        return null;
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            result[i][j] = matrix[(i + 1) % n][(j + 1) % n] - matrix[(i + 1) % n][j] + matrix[i][(j + 1) % n] - matrix[i][j];
        }
    }
    return result;
}

public static int determinant(int[][] matrix) {
    int n = matrix.length;
    if (n == 1) {
        return matrix[0][0];
    }
    int det = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int[][] subMatrix = new int[n - 1][n - 1];
        for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {
            for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                if (k != i) {
                    subMatrix[j - 1][k] = matrix[j][k];
                }
            }
        }
        det += matrix[0][i] * determinant(subMatrix);
    }
    return det;
}
```

### Example 11:
Input:
Write a Java function `public static int[][] solveLinearSystem(int[][] matrix, int[] b)` to solve a linear system of equations using Gaussian elimination.

Example:
>>> solveLinearSystem(new int[][] {{1, 2}, {3, 4}}, new int[] {5, 6})
{{1}, {2}}
Output:
```
public static int[][] solveLinearSystem(int[][] matrix, int[] b) {
    int n = matrix.length;
    int[][] result = new int[n][1];
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            int ratio = matrix[j][i] / matrix[i][i];
            for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                matrix[j][k] -= ratio * matrix[i][k];
            }
            b[j] -= ratio * b[i];
        }
    }
    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        result[i][0] = b[i];
        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            result[i][0] -= matrix[i][j] * result[j][0];
        }
        result[i][0] /= matrix[i][i];
    }
    return result;
}
```

